{{- define "custom.install.tldr" -}}
## TL;DR

```console
helm repo add {{ template "custom.repository.organization" . }} {{ template "custom.helm.url" . }}
helm repo update
helm install {{ template "chart.name" . }} {{ template "custom.helm.path" . }}
```
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.install" -}}
## Installing the Chart

To install the chart with the release name `{{ template "chart.name" . }}`

```console
helm install {{ template "chart.name" . }} {{ template "custom.helm.path" . }}
```
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.uninstall" -}}
{{- $common := false }}{{- range .Dependencies }}{{- if eq .Name "common" }}{{- $common = true }}{{- end }}{{- end -}}
## Uninstalling the Chart

To uninstall the `{{ template "chart.name" . }}` deployment

```console
helm uninstall {{ template "chart.name" . }}
```

The command removes all the Kubernetes components associated with the chart {{ if $common }}**including persistent volumes** {{ end }}and deletes the release.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.configuration.header" -}}
## Configuration
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.configuration.readValues" -}}
{{- $common := false }}{{- range .Dependencies }}{{- if eq .Name "common" }}{{- $common = true }}{{- end }}{{- end -}}
Read through the [values.yaml](./values.yaml) file. It has several commented out suggested values.
{{- if $common }}
Other values may be used from the [values.yaml]({{ template "custom.repository.url" . }}/tree/master/charts/library/common/values.yaml) from the [common library]({{ template "custom.repository.url" . }}/tree/master/charts/library/common).
{{- end }}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.configuration.example.set" -}}
{{- $common := false }}{{- range .Dependencies }}{{- if eq .Name "common" }}{{- $common = true }}{{- end }}{{- end -}}
Specify each parameter using the `--set key=value[,key=value]` argument to `helm install`.
{{- if $common }}

```console
helm install {{ template "chart.name" . }} \
  --set env.TZ="America/New_York" \
    {{ template "custom.helm.path" . }}
```
{{- end }}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.configuration.example.file" -}}
Alternatively, a YAML file that specifies the values for the above parameters can be provided while installing the chart.

```console
helm install {{ template "chart.name" . }} {{ template "custom.helm.path" . }} -f values.yaml
```
{{- end -}}

